@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Feature: Perturbation quiescence
+
+  Methodology check required on every fitting-out. A green tree carries no
+  PERTURBATION token; a standing token beside green verification is the
+  stale-green alarm the Perturbation policy names. A live plant rides
+  uncommitted with its own watchbill entries, so quiescence reddens only
+  where a standing token is a fault.
+
+  @captain @conformance
+  Scenario: No PERTURBATION token stands in implementation
+    Given the implementation directories from RIGGING.md
+    When the perturbation-quiescence check searches them for "PERTURBATION"
+    Then no standing PERTURBATION token is found
diff --git a/features/conformance/watchbill-shape.feature b/features/conformance/watchbill-shape.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4443e70
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/conformance/watchbill-shape.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Feature: Watchbill shape conformance
+
+  Methodology check required on every fitting-out. An absent watchbill
+  conforms (deck at rest); a present watchbill must match the fixed shape:
+  an object of "watchN" entries, each an object with a "scenarios" array of
+  "<spec>.feature:<Scenario Name>" references or a tier tag.
+
+  @captain @conformance
+  Scenario: Watchbill conforms to the fixed shape
+    Given the project watchbill at "watchbill.json"
+    When the watchbill-shape conformance check runs
+    Then every entry is "watchN" with a "scenarios" array of references or tier tags
+    And an absent watchbill conforms
